; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The second hero, and deliberately the first one's opposite.
;
; The archer wins at distance and loses the moment anything arrives. This one has
; no distance to win at: everything he does happens at arm's length, so the whole
; of playing him is deciding when to walk into a room rather than where to stand
; outside it. Nearly every number below is that one sentence, said in figures.
;
; Which of the two is played is DefaultHero in data/world/world.duke. There is no choosing
; screen yet; this is what makes him playable enough to be balanced.
;
; He is NOT a stronger archer. Twice the health and two thirds of the range is a
; different game, not a better hero — and if he ends up simply better, the two
; numbers to look at are AttackRange and Speed, because those are the ones that
; decide whether a mistake can be walked away from.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hero
  Name = Knight
  DisplayName = Garen
  KindOf = [INFANTRY, SELECTABLE, CAN_ATTACK]
  Geometry = Cylinder
    Radius = 5
    Height = 12
  End
  ; Wider than the archer, which is not decoration: a body's radius is what the
  ; pathfinder steers round and what a monster has to reach past. A man in plate
  ; takes up more doorway.
  ; Shorter sight than the archer's 70, and it costs him something real: the
  ; ground opens up around this number, so he walks into rooms he has seen less
  ; of. He does not need the reach — nothing he owns can hit that far — and an
  ; archer's eyes on a swordsman would be map knowledge he has not earned.
  VisionRange = 52
  Modules = [
    GrowableBody
      ; Nearly twice the archer's 550 once his twenty-two strength is on it -- 980 --
      ; and the first half of why he can stand in a room. The second half is
      ; ArmourPercent below, which is a separate axis: health is how long he
      ; lasts, armour is how much each blow is worth.
      MaxHealth = 716
    End
    MoveUpdate
      ; Slower than 29, and this is the price of the rest of the page. He cannot
      ; leave a fight he has walked into, so walking in has to be a decision.
      ; Before his agility: 19.5 and ten points at 0.15 are 21.
      Speed = 19.5
      ; 0 = turn on the spot, as the archer does. See the note in his block: a
      ; positive rate is SAGE's vehicle behaviour and makes a man drive in arcs.
      TurnRate = 0
    End
    WeaponUpdate
      ; Twice the archer's 14 a swing, and slower with it: 34 frames against 24.
      ; Worked out, that is 0.88 a frame against his 0.58 -- about half again as
      ; much damage over time, not the same amount in heavier pieces. The extra is
      ; deliberate and it is what he is paid for standing in range: everything he
      ; hits is hitting him back for the whole of it, which is not true of a single
      ; arrow the archer looses from across the room.
      ;
      ; If he turns out to be simply better, this is the second number to cut --
      ; after Speed, and before AttackRange, which is the one that makes him him.
      ;
      ; ★ Before strength, his primary, which adds its twenty-two: 30 a swing.
      Damage = 8
      ; A sword. The whole of the difference: 11 against the archer's 60, which is
      ; inside every monster's own reach rather than far outside it, so he is being
      ; hit for the whole of the time he is hitting.
      AttackRange = 11
      ReloadFrames = 34
      ; He swings as he closes, unlike a drawn bow — a swordsman who had to stop
      ; before every blow would never land one on anything that was backing away.
      AttackOnTheMove = Yes
    End
    ; No Bow and no EyesOnly: both are the archer's, and both are about a shot that
    ; has to cross a room. EyesOnly would also switch off the engine's own target
    ; acquisition, which is exactly what a creature fighting at arm's length wants
    ; left on -- there is nothing between him and what he is hitting.
    ;
    ; Walks to whatever he is told to attack — see HeroBrain, which both heroes use.
    HeroBrain
    End
    ; Q, W, E and R. Which four is in the Skill blocks at the end of this file,
    ; exactly as the archer's are in his: this line only says that he has skills.
    SkillBook
    End
    Recovery
    End
    ExperienceModule
      ExperienceValue = 0
      ExperienceRequired = [0, 0, 0]
    End
  ]


; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The knight.
;
; Out of KayKit Adventurers 2.0 (CC0), the same pack all three heroes come from,
; so the
; rig matches and every clip below retargets onto him without a thing being done
; to it. His clips come out of the Humanoid set, melee.glb among them: his swings, his
; blocks and his two-handed stance are all in that one.
;
; HE CARRIES A GREATSWORD, and that is not decoration: the pack has no
; Melee_1H_Idle, so a one-handed sword would have to stand in Melee_Unarmed_Idle
; and read as a man who has forgotten he is holding one. Two hands also suits the
; rest of him — slow, heavy, has to walk in.
;
; ★ MEASURED, NOT GUESSED. He boxes 2.543 tall against the archer's 2.275, and
; his head joint sits at 0.488 of that against the archer's 0.546 — he is a
; taller model with a proportionally smaller head. That is why his ModelScale and
; his portrait camera are not the archer's numbers, and it is the whole reason
; both are written per hero.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Title = Qalqon va qilich

  ; What he shrugs off before a single level, as a percentage. Here rather than
  ; in his creature block because a hero's armour is REWRITTEN from his level and
  ; what he has found every time either changes, so a figure in the template
  ; would not survive his first level. Counted exactly like a breastplate he
  ; found, which means the file's own floor on damage taken still holds.
  ;
  ; The second half of why he can stand in a room -- MaxHealth is the first. Two
  ; axes on purpose: health is how long he lasts and this is what each blow is
  ; worth, and a monster that hits for 8 is a different problem from one that
  ; hits for 40.
  ArmourPercent = 18

  ; He reaches 11, so he walks until he is all but touching it. The archer stops
  ; at 48 and shoots; a swordsman who did that would stand there swinging at air.
  CloseDistance = 8

  Model = models/heroes/knight.glb
  ; GeometryHeight is 12 in his template above and the model boxes 2.543 tall, so
  ; 12 / 2.543 -- measured, exactly as the archer's 5.3 was. Both heroes then
  ; stand the same height on screen, because both are 12 units of creature; what
  ; makes him look like a knight is the model, not the scale.
  ModelScale = 4.72
  Facing = 90

  ; What he moves by, as everything on two legs does; the clips below are the ones
  ; he plays his own way.
  Animations = Humanoid

  ; ★ SHIELD UP. He carries a sword and a shield now rather than two hands of
  ; greatsword, so the two-handed idle -- both fists on one hilt -- would have
  ; the shield hanging off a hand that is busy.
  ;
  ; The pack has no Melee_1H_Idle, which is why he had the greatsword in the
  ; first place. Melee_Blocking is the nearest thing to a man standing behind a
  ; shield and is what his PORTRAIT already uses for exactly that reason, so the
  ; two now agree. Melee_Unarmed_Idle is the other end of it if a permanent
  ; guard reads as too tense: arms down, which with a sword and a shield in the
  ; hands is a man at rest.
  Idle = Melee_Blocking
  ; He WALKS where the archer runs, and it is the same fact as Speed = 21 said
  ; twice: a run cycle at his pace reads as skating.
  Walk = Walking_A
  ; ★ CHOSEN BY ITS LENGTH, not by its name. The client plays this once per blow,
  ; and a blow lands every ReloadFrames -- 34, which is 1.133s. This clip runs
  ; 1.100s, so the swing FINISHES and has a breath to spare before the next.
  ;
  ; Melee_2H_Attack_Chop is the obvious pick and was the first one: it runs
  ; 1.633s, half again longer than the gap between blows, so every chop was cut
  ; off at two thirds and restarted from the top. He never once finished a swing.
  ; From a chair that reads as "the animation is bad" rather than as two numbers
  ; disagreeing.
  ;
  ; The two numbers are checked against each other in the build, so changing
  ; ReloadFrames without changing this will fail rather than look bad. _Stab is
  ; 1.600s and _Spinning is 0.667s, if the pace ever changes.
  ; ★ ONE-HANDED now, and still chosen by its LENGTH. The client plays this once
  ; per blow and a blow lands every ReloadFrames -- 34, which is 1.133s. This
  ; clip runs 1.067s, so the chop FINISHES with room to spare, which is the same
  ; test the two-handed slice passed at 1.100s.
  ;
  ; The build checks the two against each other, so changing ReloadFrames
  ; without changing this fails rather than looks bad. _Slice_Diagonal is 1.000s
  ; and _Slice_Horizontal is 1.367s (too long), if the swing ever wants changing.
  Attack = Melee_1H_Attack_Chop
  Hurt = Hit_A
  ; Death_A falls in 0.8s; Death_B takes 2.6s, which is longer than the floor
  ; stays open after he dies.
  Death = Death_A

  Held = [
    ; ★ A ONE-HANDED sword, because the other hand now has a shield in it. The
    ; greatsword is still in the folder if he ever goes back to two hands, and
    ; going back is this line plus Idle and Attack above.
    Held
      Model = models/heroes/sword_1handed.gltf
      Bone = handslot.r
      ; Body and blade came out of the same pack at the same size.
      Scale = 1
    End
    ; The RIGHT hand, unlike the rogue: he draws no string, he swings. If he ends
    ; up fighting left-handed, this is the line -- handslot.l.
    ;
    ; No HeldRoll. The bow needed half a turn because it is the one weapon in the
    ; pack laid out along its own +Z; every blade runs along +Y, which is what the
    ; hand bone is authored for.

    ; ★ AND THE SHIELD, in the hand the sword is not in. It is the second half of
    ; what makes him readable across a dark room as the one who walks in: a
    ; silhouette with a slab on one arm is not mistaken for an archer.
    ;
    ; No turn, like the sword and unlike the bow. The pack authors its own props
    ; for its own hand slots, so a shield out of this kit in this kit's hand is
    ; already the right way round -- the bow is the one documented exception in the
    ; whole set, because it is the one model laid out along +Z.
    ;
    ; ★ Worth a look all the same: it is a disc rather than a length, so the rule
    ; the build checks (longest side along +Y) has nothing to say about which way a
    ; shield FACES. If it lies flat like a tray, HeldPitch = 90 is the line.
    Held
      Model = models/heroes/shield_round.gltf
      Bone = handslot.l
      Scale = 1
    End
  ]
  ; ★ WHAT HE IS MADE OF -- see Attributes in the World block. STRENGTH is his primary: every
  ; point of it is health and swing both, and it grows fastest. At the first level
  ; these make the knight he always was: 716 + 22 x 12 = 980 health,
  ; 19.5 + 10 x 0.15 = 21 speed, 8 + 22 = 30 a swing.
  Primary = STR
  Attributes
    STR = [22, 3.0]
    AGI = [10, 1.2]
    INT = [8, 1.0]
  End
  ; ★ WHAT HE CASTS OUT OF, before his intelligence: 10 + 8 x 5 = 50. The shallowest
  ; pool in the game, and his skills are priced to match -- see his Skills.
  ; He is the hero who lives off his ordinary swing, and mana is what stops him
  ; opening with all four and then doing it again.
  MaxMana = 10
  ; Tenths of a point a second: the slowest mana of the three and the quickest
  ; mending. See the note in the Rogue's block.
  ManaRegen = 10
  HealthRegen = 20


; The knight's. Two of his states are things the archer has no clip for — a blade
; held ready, and a level worth celebrating — and the rest he shares.
;
; The camera numbers are the same as everybody's, and that is the point: they are
; fractions of whatever they are looking at, so they frame a knight by his own
; measured height without anybody having measured him. If his head comes out badly
; once his model is in, Head and Show are the two lines, and neither needs a
; rebuild.
  ; Standing with the blade, as he stands in the world.
  Portrait = PortraitArt
    Calm = Melee_2H_Idle
    ; Guarding rather than swinging: he "has a target" for a whole engagement, so a
    ; chop here would have him hacking at the air between blows.
    Fight = Melee_Blocking
    Hurt = Idle_B
    Dead = Death_A
    ; A spin, which reads as a flourish. Melee_2H_Attack_Spinning is the longer one.
    LevelUp = Melee_2H_Attack_Spin

    ; ★ NOT the archer's numbers, and this is the case the per-hero block was for.
    ; He boxes 2.543 against the archer's 2.275 and his head joint sits at 0.488 of
    ; that against 0.546 — a taller model with a proportionally smaller head — so
    ; the same fractions would frame him high and leave dead space over his helmet.
    ; Lower and a little wider: chest to just over the crest.
    Head = 0.70
    Show = 0.68
    Yaw = 22
    Pitch = -4
    Fov = 34
    HurtBelowPercent = 30
    HurtSpeed = 1.5
  End

  ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ; The knight's four, and they are the archer's four asked backwards.
  ;
  ; His are about not being reached: a shot that outranges everything, a panic
  ; button, a way out, and a window in which to spend the first two. This one has
  ; already been reached by the time any of his matter, so his are about what to do
  ; once you are standing in it — hit several things at once, arrive, survive, and
  ; keep hitting while they surround you.
  ;
  ; None of them reaches: the longest is 34, against the archer's 68. That is the
  ; whole shape of him and it is the first thing to change if he plays too safely.
  ;
  ; NO ICONS NAMED YET. A slot with no picture draws the letter of its key, which
  ; is what every slot did before there were any pictures — so he is playable now
  ; and the four lines are added when the files are. See the note over Hero
  ; Knight below for which four and where they go.
  ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Skills = [
    Skill
      Key = Q
      ; Cleave. His bread and butter: one swing that lands on the group rather than
      ; on one of them, and the reason wading in is worth doing at all.
      ;
      ; AREA_AT_SPOT rather than a cone, because a cone is a shape the game does not
      ; have and this plays as one: he aims a short way in front of himself and
      ; everything around that spot is hit. Range is how far in front he can put it —
      ; barely past his own sword — and Radius is how much of the room it covers.
      Effect = AREA_AT_SPOT
      Damage = 34
      DamagePerLevel = 6
      Range = 22
      Radius = 26
      ; Short, because it is what he does rather than something he saves.
      CooldownFrames = 75
      CooldownPerLevel = -2
      ; Four points may go into it, and it waits for nothing but one of them.
      MaxRank = 4
      ; What it looks like going off -- see Effect Cleave.
      Look = Cleave
      Name = Kesish
      Icon = icons/skills/skill_cleave.png
      Blurb = Oldidagi bir joyga zarba beradi va o'sha yerdagi hamma dushmanga tegadi. Bittasiga emas — to'daga. Uning eng tez-tez ishlatadigan mahorati.
      ManaCost = 7
      ManaCostPerLevel = 1
    End

    Skill
      Key = W
      ; Charge. How a man with eleven of reach gets to the thing he wants to hit, and
      ; the only fast thing he owns.
      ;
      ; The archer's E is the same effect saying nothing about damage, and that is
      ; the whole difference between a sprint and a charge: name a Damage and he goes
      ; THROUGH what is in the way instead of past it. Radius is how wide that path
      ; is -- a body's width, so it is the things he actually ran into.
      ;
      ; It does not shove anything aside. Pushing a body is a question about the
      ; navigation grid rather than about a skill.
      Effect = DASH
      Distance = 52
      Damage = 22
      DamagePerLevel = 4
      Radius = 14
      CooldownFrames = 165
      CooldownPerLevel = -5
      ; Four points may go into it, and it waits for nothing but one of them.
      MaxRank = 4
      ; What it looks like going off -- see Effect Charge.
      Look = Charge
      Name = Hujum
      Icon = icons/skills/skill_dash.png
      Blurb = Oldinga otiladi va yo'lida uchraganlarni ham urib o'tadi. Qo'li kalta odamning nishoniga yetadigan yagona yo'li.
      ManaCost = 12
      ManaCostPerLevel = 1
    End

    Skill
      Key = E
      ; Guard. The archer has nothing like it and should not: his answer to being
      ; surrounded is to not be there. This one cannot leave, so his answer is to be
      ; worth less to hit for a few seconds.
      ;
      ; BoostPercent is what the skill is worth, as it is for EMPOWER — there it is
      ; damage added and here it is damage avoided. Half of every blow, which sounds
      ; enormous and is four seconds long against a cooldown of eight.
      Effect = GUARD
      BoostPercent = 50
      BoostPerLevel = 2
      DurationFrames = 120
      CooldownFrames = 240
      CooldownPerLevel = -6
      ; Four points may go into it, and it waits for nothing but one of them.
      MaxRank = 4
      ; What it looks like going off -- see Effect Guard.
      Look = Guard
      Name = Qalqon
      Icon = icons/skills/skill_guard.png
      Blurb = Bir necha soniya har zarbadan kamroq zarar oladi. Kamonchida bunaqasi yo'q va bo'lmasligi ham kerak: uning javobi — o'sha yerda bo'lmaslik.
      ManaCost = 14
      ManaCostPerLevel = 0
    End

    Skill
      Key = R
      ; Whirlwind. The ultimate, and the archer's opposite again: his is a window in
      ; which everything else he does is worth more, and this one IS the thing being
      ; done — he turns for four seconds and everything near him bleeds.
      ;
      ; Damage is per landing, not per cast: TickFrames says how often it lands, so
      ; this is 14 twice a second for four seconds — 112 to anything that stays in it
      ; for the whole turn, and much less to anything that walks out. Which is the
      ; point: an ultimate that could be stepped out of is one the monsters get a say
      ; in.
      ;
      ; It follows him. Measured from wherever he is standing each time it lands, so
      ; he can carry it into the next group.
      Effect = AREA_DAMAGE
      Damage = 14
      DamagePerLevel = 2
      Radius = 34
      DurationFrames = 120
      TickFrames = 15
      CooldownFrames = 900
      CooldownPerLevel = -30
      ; Half way up the ladder, as the archer's is: the run has to be earned.
      ; Three points, and each waits for the hero: the first at level 4, the second
      ; at 8, the third at 12. A MINIMUM rather than an appointment -- pass on it at
      ; 8 and it is still there at 9.
      MaxRank = 3
      LevelPerRank = 4
      ; What it looks like going off -- see Effect Whirlwind.
      Look = Whirlwind
      Name = Girdob
      Icon = icons/skills/skill_whirlwind.png
      Blurb = To'rt soniya aylanadi va atrofidagi hamma sekin-asta qonaydi. Zarar har tushishiga hisoblanadi, shuning uchun ichida turgan ko'p oladi, chiqib ketgan kam.
      ManaCost = 30
      ManaCostPerLevel = 2
    End
  ]
End
